      "writtenOn": "2023-09-07T01:53:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I need some guidance with this one. So I believe the current logic in doing so is the following (please correct me if I am wrong @saravanak@google.com):\n\nTreat a failure as a duplicate \u003d\u003e Lesser memory allocated for the PLT section\nWe have 2 possible scenarios:\n1. Not enough memory to hold all the PLTs generated. The module is not initialized due to an error is returned from `module_emit_plt_entry` (Ref: https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/arch/arm64/kernel/module-plts.c;l\u003d94), hence the error is not ignored (IF it does cause a problem) - we simply kick the can down the road.\n2. The memory allocated is sufficient enough to hold all the PLTs generated. In which case, its OK to not handle the kmalloc error.\n\nDoes this explanation make sense? If yes, I can write a comment capturing this info.",
      "parentUuid": "3b356f8c_be46b495",
      "revId": "cb93b7f618c844e066415c8b99f37c4ae106744e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
